# 4. TEXT
 
_publ_section_abstract
; C48H200N8O104Si32, monoclinic, C2/m (No. 12), a = 16.2532(14) angstrom, b = 13.3020(7) angstrom, c = 16.7771(14) angstrom, beta = 96.476(10) degree, V = 3604.07 (3) angstrom^3, Z = 1, density = 2.02(2) g/cm3, R(F) = 0.031, chi2 = 2.44, T = 293 K.
;

_publ_section_exptl_
; RUB-56 samples were hydrothermally synthesized in Teflon-lined autoclaves at 140 degree C for 2-7 days using diethyldimethylammonium hydroxide (Sigma-Aldrich, 20% in water) as the structure directing agent (SDA). Reaction mixtures of composition 0.9-1 SiO2 : 0.5 SDA : 6-10 H2O were used. Lab-made silica gel (11 wt% H2O) served as the silica source. A more detailed view on the synthesis of RUB-56 is presented in a patent application [1]. The sample of highest crystallinity with respect to purity and (small) halfwidths of the diffraction peaks was used for the structure analysis. 
;

_publ_section_exptl_refinement
